---
description: Searchable entity pickers use PrimeNG p-select with filter — never modals or one-off autocomplete UX
alwaysApply: true
---

# Combo search select (searchable dropdown)

When the user needs to **pick one record from a list** (people, tasks, clients, projects, etc.), use the same **filterable `p-select`** pattern used elsewhere in the admin app. Do **not** introduce modals, popovers, or bare `p-autocomplete` for these flows unless the feature is explicitly the global top-bar search.

## Default control

- **`p-select`** with `[filter]="true"`, `filterBy="…"`, `filterPlaceholder="Search…"`, `[showClear]="true"`, `appendTo="body"`, `styleClass="w-full"`.
- Load **options upfront** (API or computed signals). User opens the dropdown and types to filter — no minimum character count, no “search to see anything.”
- After selection: run the action (e.g. add row), then **clear** the bound value so the control stays a “pick again” field (`setTimeout(() => pickId = null)` if needed).

## Reference implementations

| Use case | Where to copy |
|----------|----------------|
| Task picker on a form | `admin/src/app/pages/time-entry/time-entry-modal.component.ts` — Work task `p-select` |
| **Person** (CRM / team, avatar rows) | **`app-people-select`** + `PeoplePickerLoader` — Add person (existing tab), project contacts, Task Share. Do not hand-roll another people `p-select`. |
| Person / static lists (simple label only) | `project-form.page.html` — Client `p-select` (no avatar) |
| Static / already-loaded lists | `admin/src/app/pages/projects/project-form.page.html` — Client `p-select` |

## Rich rows (avatar, subtitle)

Every picker row is **`app-pick-row`**: avatar (people) or icon (records), bold title, secondary line underneath — always two lines. For **people**, use **`app-people-select`** (see `ui-reuse-RRY.mdc`). For other entities, put `app-pick-row` in the `#item` template; if a second screen needs the same row layout, extract a shared component first (RRY).

```html
<p-select
  [options]="options()"
  optionLabel="label"
  optionValue="id"
  [(ngModel)]="pickId"
  (ngModelChange)="onPick($event)"
  [filter]="true"
  filterBy="label,email,firstName,lastName"
  filterPlaceholder="Search…"
  [showClear]="true"
  [loading]="loading()"
  placeholder="Search and select…"
  styleClass="w-full"
  appendTo="body"
>
  <ng-template #item let-option>
    <app-pick-row [icon]="'pi-folder'" [title]="option.label" [subtitle]="option.clientName" />
  </ng-template>
</p-select>
```

## Cross-system people lists

- API: `GET /search/people?limit=250` (optional `q`, `excludeProjectId`). Implementation: `api/src/app/search/people-directory.service.ts`.
- Sort **last name, then first name**; show **First Last** (title) with the **email underneath** (secondary line). No email → `No email on file`.

## Do not

- `p-dialog` / modal pickers for “choose one from a list”
- `p-autocomplete` with `minLength={2}` as the only way to see options
- Custom popover pickers when `p-select` + filter suffices
- New UI patterns without checking the references above first
